## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross‑protocol data models and practical adapters.

## Key Concepts
- Shared domain model across REST, GraphQL, and gRPC
- Versioned contracts and simple compatibility rules
- Per-protocol adapters and a unified error envelope
- Tenant-aware contract loading for OpenAPI

## Code Example
```yaml
openapi: 3.0.0
info: {title: User service, version: v1}
paths:
  /users/{id}:
    get: { responses: { '200': { description: OK, content: { 'application/json': { schema: { $ref: '#/components/schemas/User' } } }}}}}
components:
  schemas:
    User:
      type: object
      properties:
        id: { type: string }
        name: { type: string }
        email: { type: string }
```
```graphql
type User {
  id: ID!
  name: String!
  email: String!
}
```
```proto
message User {
  string id = 1;
  string name = 2;
  string email = 3;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test cross‑protocol compatibility during CI?
- How would you handle breaking schema changes across REST/GraphQL/gRPC?

